S9 \emdash  FIRESTORE PRO STATUS SYNC (Cursor Spec)\par
===========================================\par
\par
Sprint goal: Mirror the user\'92s Pro status into Firestore so it can be used for team\par
feature checks and manual Pro grants from the Firebase console. StoreKit remains the\par
authoritative source for feature gating \emdash  Firestore is a mirror + manual override only.\par
\par
CRITICAL RULES (never violate):\par
\bullet  StoreKit always wins for feature gating in the app. Never gate features on Firestore isPro alone.\par
\bullet  Never set isPro = true anywhere in code (revert before App Store build).\par
\bullet  Use modelContext.safeSave(context:) \emdash  never try? modelContext.save()\par
\par
---\par
\par
FIRESTORE DOCUMENT STRUCTURE:\par
Collection: "users"\par
Document ID: Firebase Auth uid\par
\par
Fields to add (merge, never overwrite full document):\par
    isPro: Bool              \emdash  mirrors current StoreKit entitlement status\par
    manualProUntil: Timestamp?  \emdash  if present and in the future, grants Pro regardless of StoreKit\par
\par
No other subscription fields needed. Keep it minimal.\par
\par
---\par
\par
ITEM S9-1 \emdash  Add Firestore Pro sync methods to FirestoreManager\par
File: AITest/Models/FirestoreManager.swift\par
\par
Add two new methods:\par
\par
// Writes the current isPro status to the user\'92s Firestore document.\par
// Called every time SubscriptionManager resolves StoreKit entitlements.\par
func writeProStatus(_ isPro: Bool) \{\par
    guard let uid = Auth.auth().currentUser?.uid else \{ return \}\par
    let db = Firestore.firestore()\par
    db.collection("users").document(uid).setData(\par
        ["isPro": isPro],\par
        merge: true\par
    ) \{ error in\par
        if let error = error \{\par
            print("[Firestore] Failed to write isPro: \\(error.localizedDescription)")\par
        \}\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\par
// Fetches manualProUntil from Firestore. Returns true if a valid future date exists.\par
// Called once on app launch and after sign-in.\par
func fetchManualProGrant() async -> Bool \{\par
    guard let uid = Auth.auth().currentUser?.uid else \{ return false \}\par
    let db = Firestore.firestore()\par
    do \{\par
        let doc = try await db.collection("users").document(uid).getDocument()\par
        if let timestamp = doc.data()?["manualProUntil"] as? Timestamp \{\par
            return timestamp.dateValue() > Date()\par
        \}\par
    \} catch \{\par
        print("[Firestore] Failed to fetch manualProUntil: \\(error.localizedDescription)")\par
    \}\par
    return false\par
\}\par
\par
