\par
2. In AuthManager, after a successful sign-in (Google, Apple, Email), add:\par
       Task \{ await SubscriptionManager.shared.applyManualProGrantIfNeeded() \}\par
\par
The result: if an admin sets manualProUntil in Firebase console to a future date,\par
the user gets isPro = true on next app launch or sign-in automatically.\par
\par
---\par
\par
HOW TO MANUALLY GRANT PRO FROM FIREBASE CONSOLE:\par
1. Open Firebase Console \emdash  Firestore \emdash  users collection\par
2. Find the user\'92s document by their UID (visible in Firebase Auth)\par
3. Add or update the field: manualProUntil (type: timestamp) \emdash  set to desired expiry date\par
4. User gets Pro access on next app launch. No code deploy needed.\par
To revoke: delete the manualProUntil field or set it to a past date.\par
\par
