S18 \emdash  RELIABLE LANGUAGE SWITCH + FULL LOCALIZATION COVERAGE (Cursor Spec)\par
===========================================\par
Sprint goal: Fix the two remaining localization defects from Tamil/Hindi device QA:\par
(1) switching language mid-session leaves HALF the UI in the old language;\par
(2) many labels (whole Paywall, Dashboard, StorageDetail, etc.) stay ENGLISH because they are rendered from String variables/interpolation, which SwiftUI does NOT localize.\par
Diagnosis is quantified: literals are all in the catalog (0 missing), but there are ~125 Text(variable) UI labels + ~108 interpolated Text that bypass localization across ~58 files.\par
\par
CRITICAL RULES (never violate):\par
- Use modelContext.safeSave(context:) \emdash  never try? modelContext.save()\par
- Never set isPro = true in any code\par
- Never add NavigationStack inside a sheet/modal that already has one\par
- Never introduce free-trial language anywhere (Stoqly has NO free trial)\par
- Keep accessibilityIdentifier values English/stable (Maestro hooks)\par
- Do NOT translate DATA: item/storage/template names, categories, UOM symbols, SKUs, barcodes, StoreKit product.displayName/displayPrice, currency symbols. ONLY localize UI labels/messages.\par
\par
\emdash \par
\par
ITEM S18-1 \emdash  Make language switching reliable (fix the half-old/half-new bug)\par
Root cause: LocalizationManager.setLanguage bumps refreshID and the root uses .id(refreshID), but .id() on a child view does NOT tear down presented sheets, NavigationStack destinations, or @StateObject-cached strings, so those keep the previous language. Bundle-swizzle + .id() is unreliable for mid-session switch.\par
Fix (primary \emdash  full window re-root):\par
- On setLanguage(): after updating storedCode + Bundle.setLanguage + AppleLanguages, DISMISS any presented sheet/navigation, then RE-ROOT the key window:\par
    - get the active UIWindowScene from UIApplication.shared.connectedScenes, its keyWindow,\par
    - set window.rootViewController = UIHostingController(rootView: ContentView()... with the same environmentObjects + .environment(\\.locale, ...) + .environment(\\.layoutDirection, ...)),\par
    - optional: a short cross-dissolve transition for polish.\par
  This rebuilds the ENTIRE tree (and drops stale sheets) so every string re-resolves in the new language.\par
- Keep .environment(\\.locale, effectiveLocale()) and the Bundle override; the re-root makes both take effect everywhere.\par
- Fallback (only if re-root proves flaky): show a one-line "Restart Stoqly to apply the language" note after switching. Prefer the re-root.\par
Test: Tamil -> switch to Hindi -> 100% Hindi immediately (no Tamil remnants), including Dashboard, Settings, and any open sheet.\par
\par
ITEM S18-2 \emdash  Localize variable-rendered UI labels (the English-text bug)\par
Use the audit script as the checklist:\par
    python3 AITest/Localization/localization_audit.py --all\par
It lists Text(variable) "LIKELY UI LABELS" (~125) and interpolated Text (~108), grouped by file, EXCLUDING data vars.\par
For each LABEL case, localize at the source:\par
  (a) Fixed label held in a String property/struct -> change the property TYPE to LocalizedStringKey and keep the literal; Text(prop) then localizes. (Best for enums/structs of feature rows, tips, KPI titles, etc.)\par
  (b) Runtime string whose value is a known catalog key -> Text(LocalizedStringKey(value)).\par
