Problem: the in-app Language picker changes Text/LocalizedStringKey (via .environment(\\.locale)) but NOT imperative String(localized:) calls (Inventory Health, Needs Attention, Go Pro strip, Sales Performance, etc.). Those follow the DEVICE/process language, so on a non-Tamil phone they stay English. Root cause: String(localized:) does not read the SwiftUI environment locale, and the Bundle swizzle does not intercept the modern String(localized:) API. Catalog is fine \u2014 all strings ARE translated.\par
\par
Fix (CEO-chosen): apply the language on RELAUNCH, exactly like iOS per-app language. After relaunch the PROCESS language is the chosen one, so BOTH Text and String(localized:) resolve correctly \u2014 no swizzle tricks, no half-translated screens.\par
