S27 \emdash  EDIT / DELETE past sales & movements (with 7-day window) (Cursor Spec)\par
===========================================\par
Goal: let users FIX mistaken sales/movement entries. Phase 1 = DELETE/REVERSE (ship first). Phase 2 = in-place EDIT (fast-follow, spec at bottom). From BOTH the Sales list and the Movements list. Time-limited to protect current stock + historical reports.\par
\par
WHY the window: deleting/editing a sale REVERSES stock. Reversing an OLD entry corrupts current inventory (item has been recounted/sold many times since) and rewrites past reports. So entries are editable/deletable only for a short recent period.\par
\par
CONFIG: add `enum EditPolicy \{ static let windowDays = 7 \}` (Constants.swift). An entry is editable/deletable only if Date().timeIntervalSince(record.createdAt) <= windowDays*86400. (Use createdAt = when entered.) Older \u2192 locked (read-only). Keep it a single constant so it can be tuned / moved to Settings later.\par
\par
CRITICAL RULES: safeSave(context:); **insert the ActivityEvent BEFORE any modelContext.delete**; never isPro=true; no free-trial; new UI strings via catalog (then run translate_catalog.py); Firestore sync every touched record.\par
\par
\emdash  PHASE 1: DELETE / REVERSE (ship now) \emdash \par
\par
ITEM S27-1 \emdash  SaleEvent delete/reverse helper\par
Add SaleHelpers.reverseSale(_ sale: SaleEvent, modelContext:):\par
1. Guard within window (else no-op / caller hides the action).\par
2. If sale.item != nil:\par
   - Insert ActivityEvent "SaleReversed" (BEFORE deletes): itemName, storageName, quantityBefore = item.currentQuantity, quantityAfter = item.currentQuantity + sale.quantitySold; sync activity.\par
   - item.currentQuantity += sale.quantitySold; item.updatedAt = now; FirestoreManager.syncItem(item).\par
3. Delete the linked movement: find InventoryMovement where linkedSaleEventId == sale.id -> modelContext.delete + Firestore delete.\par
4. Delete the SaleEvent -> modelContext.delete + Firestore delete.\par
5. safeSave(context: "ReverseSale").\par
- If sale.item == nil (item deleted): skip stock change; still delete sale + linked movement + audit.\par
\par
ITEM S27-2 \emdash  InventoryMovement delete/reverse helper\par
Add SaleHelpers.reverseMovement(_ m: InventoryMovement, modelContext:):\par
- If m.linkedSaleEventId != nil: BLOCK \u2014 this movement belongs to a sale; caller shows "Part of a sale \u2014 edit from the Sales list." Do not delete independently (avoids double-reversal).\par
- Standalone movement (manual purchase/adjustment/waste), within window:\par
   - Insert ActivityEvent "MovementReversed" first.\par
   - Reverse stock: IN -> item.currentQuantity -= m.quantity; OUT -> += m.quantity (guard item != nil); updatedAt; syncItem.\par
   - Delete movement -> modelContext.delete + Firestore delete. safeSave.\par
\par
ITEM S27-3 \emdash  UI: Sales list + Movements list\par
- SalesView: tap a sale row -> SaleDetailView (new) showing full sale + a red "Delete / Reverse" button (only if within window; else a "Locked \u2014 entered more than 7 days ago" note). Confirmation alert: "Reverse this sale? The stock will be added back." Also add swipeActions delete on the row (same guard + confirm).\par
- MovementsListView: tap a row -> MovementDetailView (new) with Delete (standalone only; linked-to-sale rows show the "edit from Sales" note). Same window guard + confirm.\par
- After delete: dismiss, show a toast, list refreshes (SwiftData @Query auto-updates).\par
