S39 --  Live language switch: fix stuck String(localized:) labels, then remove restart prompt (Cursor Spec)\par
\par
SUPERSEDES S38 Item 2 (which was insufficient -- see WHY).\par
\par
===========================================\par
\par
WHY: Founder confirmed some labels (e.g. "Inventory Health" on the Dashboard) stay in the PREVIOUS language after an in-app language switch, which is why the "Restart to apply" prompt was kept. Root cause: the app switches language by swizzling Bundle.main (LocalizedBundle overrides localizedString(forKey:value:table:)). That swizzle is honored by Text(LocalizedStringKey) / NSLocalizedString, so plain Text("...") labels DO switch live. But String(localized:) (the iOS 15+ String.LocalizationValue API) resolves via LocalizedStringResource and BYPASSES the swizzle -- it follows the DEVICE language, so those labels stay stuck. There are 265 String(localized:) call sites. Fixing them makes the live switch complete, after which the restart prompt can be removed (root already has .id(localizationManager.refreshID) + environment locale, so a rebuild re-resolves everything).\par
\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
ITEM 1 -- Add an override-bundle-backed localized-string helper\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
1. In LocalizationManager (AITest/Utilities/LocalizationManager.swift) add:\par
     var currentBundle: Bundle \{\par
         guard let code = currentCode,\par
               let path = Bundle.main.path(forResource: code, ofType: "lproj")\par
                 ?? Bundle.main.path(forResource: String(code.split(separator: "-").first ?? ""), ofType: "lproj"),\par
               let b = Bundle(path: path)\par
         else \{ return .main \}\par
         return b\par
     \}\par
   (Reuse the same lproj-resolution logic as Bundle+Localization.localizedBundle(for:); factor it into one shared function if cleaner.)\par
2. Add a global helper (new file AITest/Utilities/LocalizedString.swift):\par
     import Foundation\par
     /// Resolves against the in-app language override bundle so it follows the\par
     /// in-app switch (unlike String(localized:), which follows the device language).\par
     @inline(__always) func L(_ key: String, _ fallback: String) -> String \{\par
         LocalizationManager.shared.currentBundle.localizedString(forKey: key, value: fallback, table: nil)\par
     \}\par
\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
ITEM 2 -- Replace ALL String(localized:) UI call sites with L(...)\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
Mechanically convert every String(localized:) that produces a user-facing label (all 265):\par
  String(localized: "KEY", defaultValue: "DEFAULT")                 -> L("KEY", "DEFAULT")\par
  String(format: String(localized: "KEY", defaultValue: "D %@"), x) -> String(format: L("KEY", "D %@"), x)\par
  navigationTitle(String(localized: "KEY", defaultValue: "D"))      -> navigationTitle(L("KEY", "D"))\par
  Text(String(localized: "KEY", defaultValue: "D"))                 -> Text(L("KEY", "D"))\par
Notes:\par
  - Drop any `comment:`/`table:` args (dev-only); keep key + defaultValue.\par
  - Where a key has NO defaultValue in source, use the key itself as fallback: L("KEY", "KEY") -- but prefer to supply the real English string if present in the catalog.\par
  - Do NOT touch plain Text("literal") / Text(LocalizedStringKey) -- those already switch live via the swizzle.\par
  - Highest-count files to sweep first: SaleAndMovementDetailViews (28), DashboardView (20), FeedbackView (19), ActivityEvent (18), SubscriptionManager (14), FilteredItemListView (12), NotificationSettingsView (11), ReportsView (10), HelpCentreView (10), InventoryMovement (10). Then the rest until `grep -rn "String(localized:" AITest --include=*.swift | grep -v build` returns 0.\par
  - Enum/model files (ActivityEvent, InventoryMovement) that expose localized display strings: make them computed (not stored) and use L(...), so they re-resolve on rebuild.\par
