ITEM 1 -- Arabic does not flip to RTL on in-app language switch\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
BUG: Switching to Arabic updates the text (S39 works) but the layout stays left-to-right. Other languages are fine.\par
ROOT CAUSE: The app only sets SwiftUI's .environment(\\.layoutDirection, ...) (AITestApp + AppWindowCoordinator). On an IN-APP language change (device stays LTR), that alone does not flip the live UIKit-hosted hierarchy (nav bars, hosting controller, back chevron, alignment). There is NO semanticContentAttribute set anywhere. iOS only adopts app-wide RTL when the app actually runs in Arabic (AppleLanguages) after a relaunch -- which S39 intentionally removed.\par
