S46 --  Fix ITMS-91064 (app privacy manifest tracking/domains mismatch) + anomaly audit (Cursor Spec)\par
\par
===========================================\par
\par
ROOT CAUSE (confirmed): AITest/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy has NSPrivacyTracking=true but NSPrivacyTrackingDomains is EMPTY. Apple's rule is bidirectional: if NSPrivacyTracking=true you MUST list >=1 tracking domain (the ITMS-91064 message text is misleadingly one-directional). The empty array was introduced earlier to stop an FBSDK debug crash; that is what caused the App Store rejection of builds 6 and 7.\par
\par
APPLY THE FIX:\par
- Keep NSPrivacyTracking=true (correct: app uses ATT + Meta App Events + AdMob + analytics; collected-data types are flagged as used for tracking).\par
- Set NSPrivacyTrackingDomains to the app's REAL tracking domain(s) -- verify which the app actually connects to before choosing. Likely accurate candidates for this stack: "app-measurement.com" (Firebase/GA4), the AdMob ad/conversion domain(s), and/or Amplitude endpoints. Pick the ones the app genuinely hits.\par
- CRITICAL: Do NOT list facebook.com or ANY facebook subdomain (e.g. ep1.facebook.com) in the APP manifest. FBSDK pre-declares its own facebook tracking domains in FBSDK's OWN manifest; duplicating them in the app manifest re-triggers the FBSDK domain-error DEBUG crash we fixed earlier. Apple aggregates domains across all manifests, so Meta is already covered by FBSDK's manifest. (If Meta's domain MUST be in the app manifest for some reason, also set FBSDKCoreKit Settings.shared.isDomainErrorEnabled=false before SDK init -- but the preferred fix is simply to list a non-facebook tracking domain.)\par
- Remember: any domain listed here becomes ATT-gated (connections blocked until the user grants tracking), so only list genuine tracking domains.\par
\par
ALSO ANALYSE FOR ANOMALIES (report findings; do not guess):\par
1. Enumerate the exact tracking domains the app connects to (from the integrated SDKs + their endpoints) so the listed domain(s) are accurate, not assumed.\par
2. Consistency: Device ID / Product Interaction / Purchase History are marked NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking=true. Confirm that matches the app's real data use AND matches the App Store Connect privacy "nutrition label". If the app does NOT actually use these for cross-app tracking, the alternative is NSPrivacyTracking=false + those tracking flags false + empty domains -- but only if that's truthful. Recommend which is correct.\par
3. Bundling: confirm AITest/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy is actually a member/resource of the SmartInventory app target and lands at the .app ROOT when built (a prior build showed NO app-root PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy -- verify this is fixed). Confirm there is exactly ONE app-level manifest (no stale/duplicate copies).\par
4. Source control: the file is currently UNTRACKED in git (git status shows "?? AITest/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"). Commit it so clean/CI builds include the corrected manifest.\par
5. Required-reason APIs: verify NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes is complete (UserDefaults CA92.1 present; check whether the app also needs entries for File timestamp, System boot time, Disk space, or Active keyboard reasons).\par
6. Facebook SDK version: Package.resolved still pins facebook-ios-sdk 17.4.0 (the intended 18.x update never applied -- likely the SPM version rule is pinned). This is UNRELATED to ITMS-91064; flag whether to actually update it or leave it, and note that updating won't fix this rejection.\par
\par
VERIFY (post-fix, before uploading):\par
- Clean build + archive. Inspect the archived app's manifests:\par
    ARCHIVE=$(ls -dt ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives/*/*.xcarchive | head -1)\par
    APP=$(ls -d "$ARCHIVE/Products/Applications/"*.app)\par
    find "$APP" -name "*.xcprivacy" | while read f; do echo "== $\{f#$APP/\} =="; plutil -extract NSPrivacyTracking raw "$f" 2>/dev/null; plutil -extract NSPrivacyTrackingDomains json "$f" 2>/dev/null; done\par
  Confirm the app-root PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy now shows tracking=true + a NON-empty, non-facebook domain list, and NO manifest has a domains/tracking mismatch.\par
- Bump to Build 8 and re-submit.\par
